  "license_note": "Public domain / CC BY 4.0 as stated by the Climate Hazards Center and the Scientific Data descriptor. Cite the dataset and record the access date.",
  "limitations": [
    "This is a simple percentage anomaly of accumulated precipitation, not a calibrated drought index.",
    "It must not be used alone to classify drought severity; the same percentage anomaly has different meaning in different climates and seasons.",
    "The observation window and every baseline window cover the same calendar months (whole months only) and come from the same product (CHIRPS v3 Final).",
    "The baseline is the mean of complete yearly window totals; years with any missing month are excluded, not imputed.",
    "The baseline uses only 10 years, shorter than the 30-year length commonly used for climatologies; the baseline mean is less stable.",
    "CHIRPS v3 is a satellite-and-station blended gridded estimate at 0.05 degrees (roughly 5 km), land only. A point value is the value of the containing grid cell, not a gauge measurement.",
    "Published validation covers selected regions. This project has performed no validation of CHIRPS v3 at the requested location.",
    "Station density varies strongly by region and period; sparsely gauged or gap-filled areas are more uncertain (see CHC station-density and fill-map diagnostics).",
    "CHIRPS v3 applies gauge-undercatch correction and is systematically somewhat wetter than CHIRPS v2. Do not mix versions within one baseline or comparison.",
    "Only the Final product is used. Recent months may be unavailable until published."
  ]
